  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Caryptoside and Neuropilin-2, as all three paths point to a common intermediate, MIP, which is targeted by different compounds—Sansalvamide A, Schisanhenol B, and Poricoic Acid B. These compounds are all predicted to interact with MIP, which in turn is targeted by Neuropilin-2. The final scores across the three paths are consistent, indicating a reliable relationship across different chemical structures. The shared target MIP implies that the mode of action of these compounds may involve similar molecular interactions, potentially through a common pathway or mechanism. The evidence supports the hypothesis that Caryptoside may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by targeting MIP, and thus influencing Neuropilin-2. The integration of these paths highlights the potential for Caryptoside to modulate Neuropilin-2 through a shared target, reinforcing the clinical relevance of this relationship.",
